From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 14:33:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/28] self-hosted: expose shared-base HTTP admission

Use HTTP_SERVER_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS for both local-backend HTTP entry points, reject malformed, zero, or unsupported values before runtime and database initialization, and pass the setting through self-hosted Compose. Remove the fixed 128-request backend cap and fixed four-request HTTP action proxy cap.

Treat HTTP_SERVER_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS minus HTTP_SERVER_DEPENDENCY_RESERVE as shared base occupancy consumed by every request. Permit only callback-token-bearing /api/actions requests above that base, preserve FIFO while base capacity is available, and keep total occupancy bounded by the configured maximum.

Track actual permit waits with dependency-class waiter gauges and a duration histogram. Initialize both waiter labels for every HTTP service at zero so the sampled gauge remains an explicit compatibility anchor while histogram count, sum, and buckets retain waits shorter than the scrape interval.

Place admission outside request instrumentation and timeout, bound direct constructor values, cover cancellation and waiter-guard handoff, and centralize the callback-token header contract. Document pre-permit waiting, response-stream permit lifetime, finite callback depth, reverse-proxy requirements, and the independent relationship with isolate-scheduler overflow.
